Z||000003||fiero56||11-14-1999||06:28 PM||||For those of you who were lucky enough to get a chance to go to the Columbus nationals, there was a guy showing off his northstar setup.  It was sweet.  He had these WIDE rear tires, a good foot wide, maybe more. When he hit the has he'd break 'em loose and end up steering sideways.  Was very cool.  <BR>It was that purple "rebody" out towards the street oppostite of the entrance.  Near the 85GT? that was having the fuel pump replaced.||||reg||14
Z||000004||88formula||11-14-1999||06:36 PM||||I saw those northstar fieros in HRM also, and they mentioned in the article that the purple one could do the quarter mile in 11.2 seconds with no juice on.||||reg||1
Z||000005||olympic||11-14-1999||07:44 PM||||There was a northstar equipped 87 fiero in Kit Car magazine not long ago. He had the 300 hp version with 3.71 gears and a 100 HP shot of nitrous. The car also had an IMSA wide body kit and an over-the-roof scoop. They didnt mention a quarter mile time but the car did 0-60 mph in 4.8 sec without nitrous!!!!  If I'm not mistaken this is as fast as a Viper!!!  <BR>  I emailed American Custom Engineering a while back and asked them why their web site said that the northstar wasn't a good candidate for nitrous or a turbo. They said that the engine was designed to be super light weight(it weighs less than the iron duke) and have a max of 300 HP. The block and rotating assembly can't take a big increase in pressure. The most boost that they recommended was 4 psi.(I'm pretty sure that the twin turbo version that Cadillac will use at LeMans is very heavily modified internally.) ACE also recommended the 3.8 V6 if you desire an engine which would accept large amounts of performance upgrades.<BR>   I also read somewhere that the rear spaceframe of a fiero was only strong enough to hold about 300Hp. Did anyone else see this? Yes I know that there are people who would mount a 900Hp big block up to a getrag 5 speed and claim the car handled it. But the tranny can only transmit about 250 Hp to the wheels.  ||||reg||1
